          {
            title: '1000 (Tysiąc)',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "TysiÄ…c ('Thousand') is Poland's national card game. 2-4 players. 24-card deck (9-A). Auction bidding + melding + trick-taking. Melds: K+Q same suit = 'marriage' (â™¥=100, â™¦=80, â™£=60, â™ =40). Declaring a marriage makes that suit trump. Card points: A=11, 10=10, K=4, Q=3, J=2, 9=0. Total 120. First to 1000 wins. Musik (talon) taken by bid winner.",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "1000 (Tysiacha/Tysiąc) is a point-trick marriage game well known across Eastern Europe—Russia, Belarus, Ukraine, Kazakhstan, Poland, and Lithuania. In Russian it is Tysiacha (Тысяча), in Polish Tysiąc; both mean 'thousand,' the target score. Slight rule variations exist between and within countries; the Polish form Tysiąc licytowany (Auction 1000) is widely played as Poland's national card game.",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '3 (2-4 variants)',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '24 cards: 9-J-Q-K-10-A (ranking). 7 each + 3-card musik.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Cards, scorepad',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '7 each + 3-card musik (talon).',
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
      },
    ],
